    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d762">

                <pb facs="1044" n="924" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg924"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2780: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Child</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-26T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                                1922—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>156. Your 203, October 24, 10 p.m.</p>
                <p>You will advise Foreign Office as indicated in Department’s No. 147, via
                        Paris,<anchor n="11" xml:id="d762-f1"/> omitting references in text to
                    Italy’s failure to reply and adding that the Governments of Japan and France
                    have already expressed their concurrence in this Government’s proposal to wind
                    up Inter-Allied Technical Board on October 31.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d762-f1" n="11" xml:id="d762-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 311, Oct. 13, to the Ambassador in France, <ref target="#pg920"
                        >p. 920</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
